Reference retarget (the pick cursor)
description: the pointer_pick_editing state
- >
  Enter on a committed atom (atom_focused) opened its reference for editing - the pick cursor
  (state.ts): the pointer STAYS in the document while it edits behind the projected `*` (no
  remove+insert churn against the sync flush). The raw decomposes into the SAME segment cells the
  entry face uses (grammar/portions.ts portionsOfRaw seeds the ladder and the cells from the
  committed spelling), with the same grammar: `:` splits, `[` folds an index, Backspace merges /
  descends the scope, and the optional completion hints (complete.ts) advise over the active
  cell - the server host's provider is the live tree, the pure editor's the in-memory document.
  The server mount claims the shared TOC FILTER SESSION here too (yed-toc-pick.ts): the typed
  query prunes the TOC, and a TOC row click spells the picked path into the cells (the
  retarget's holder, the typed ladder) - inserted, never committed.
  Commit JOINS the segments and parses-or-refuses; an UNCHANGED raw commits as a no-op (an
  unasked spelling rewrite never reaches the disk); leaving with arrows commits too - garbage
  refuses the move. Abandonment needs no wiring: clicking another cell moves the cursor and the
  un-committed edit simply never lands (the document held the OLD pointer throughout).
- !!<*yamlover: $defs: table>
  header:
    - Event
      width: 2
    - 'Condition / note'
      width: 4
    - 'Next state'
      width: 2
  - ['`alphanumeric`', 'native text in the active segment cell', '`pointer_pick_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`colon`', 'the empty first cell climbs the scope; otherwise the segment commits, the next opens', '`pointer_pick_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`open_bracket`', 'an empty non-first cell - an index folds onto the previous segment', '`pointer_pick_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`hint_pick`', 'a dropdown row replaces the active cell''s text; Enter still commits', '`pointer_pick_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`toc_click`', 'the server mount only (yed-toc-pick.ts): the picked path spells into the cells (the retarget''s holder, the typed ladder) - inserted; Enter still commits', '`pointer_pick_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`enter`', 'the joined raw parses (or stands unchanged) - the retarget lands and Enter walks the SIBLING rule', '[entry_hole](*::server:yamlover-editor:entry_hole)']
  - ['`enter`', 'not a pointer the wire can carry', '[error_flash](*::server:yamlover-editor:error_flash)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'at the head of a non-first segment - the cells merge; the first cell''s head descends the scope', '`pointer_pick_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'the emptied floor - the REFERENCE goes, the entry''s name survives as the named hole (removeLevel)', '[entry_hole](*::server:yamlover-editor:entry_hole)']
  - ['`backspace`', 'otherwise', '`pointer_pick_editing` (stays)']
  - ['`tab`', 'block rows: indent/dedent (refused on a committed row, visibly); flow: the walk', '']
  - ['`up_arrow`', '', '[focus_prev](*::server:yamlover-editor:focus_prev)']
  - ['`down_arrow`', '', '[focus_next](*::server:yamlover-editor:focus_next)']
